{"change_summary":"Strengthened `probe_thermal_suppression` in `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs` so the 25 C control must demonstrate actual breeding before the heat-stress arm can pass, and updated the shrimp summary path to persist successful `trace.jsonl` artifacts and print their deterministic locations in the report. The thermal comparison now prefers offspring or hatch evidence over the old readiness-only fallback when reproductive evidence exists, closing the case where both tanks could stop breeding and still pass as long as the warm arm looked slightly worse.","outstanding_risks":["The thermal probe still depends on the seeded berried-female fixture plus the first-day 25->31 C heat shock; substantial future retunes to hatch timing or thermal egg-drop behavior may require the scenario window or seed state to be adjusted.","Successful summary traces are written to deterministic temp directories under `/tmp/tank_harness`, so rerunning the same seeded summary probe overwrites the previous success artifact bundle for that scenario label.","The worktree still contains unrelated pre-existing modifications in `.claude/worktrees/tanksim-6e5.4.7`, `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs`, `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs`, `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs`, `crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs`, and `.ralph-burning/`; they were left untouched."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspect the pending amendments in the shrimp probe suite, confirm the thermal arm currently relied on a readiness fallback, and verify the summary runner already had deterministic artifact paths available for success-side trace persistence.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Patch `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs` so the summary path persists success artifacts and reports their `trace.jsonl` paths, and so `probe_thermal_suppression` records hatch counts, compares offspring or hatch evidence when available, and fails if the cool control never produces hatch evidence or offspring.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Run targeted harness validation plus the full shrimp scenario probe suite, then verify that the summary run really left the expected success-side trace files on disk.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo test -p tank_harness successful_runs_can_persist_artifacts_for_summary_reporting -- --nocapture` passed; the harness-level success-artifact persistence check stayed green.","`cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes -- --nocapture` passed; all 6 tests succeeded, and `probe_thermal_suppression` now reported `cool_hatches=9`, `warm_hatches=0`, `cool_juv=218`, `warm_juv=0`, proving the cool control is a working breeding baseline.","The same shrimp-suite run printed summary report entries with persisted trace paths for every scenario, e.g. `breeding_success=/tmp/tank_harness/breeding_success_shrimp_successful_breeding_summary_seed6600/trace.jsonl` and paired warm/cool thermal trace paths.","`rg --files /tmp/tank_harness | rg 'summary_seed660[0-4]/trace\\.jsonl$'` returned 8 summary trace files, covering breeding, chemistry stress, crash mode, both thermal arms, and all three chloride-protection branches."]}